CHAPTER.VERS:
Rise up, you

          {+}
         women who are at ease, [and] hear my voice; you

          {+}
         careless daughters, give ear to my speech.

For days beyond a year you

          {+}
         will be troubled, you

          {+}
         careless women; for the vintage will fail, the ingathering will not come.

Tremble, you

          {+}
         women who are at ease; be troubled, you

          {+}
         careless ones; strip

          {+}
        , and make yourselves bare, and gird [sackcloth] on your

          {+}
         loins.

Blessed are you

          {+}
         who sow beside all waters, who send forth the feet of the ox and the donkey.
